WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.295
Running Learn's commands offline
shows what they don't do,

2
00:00:03.295 --> 00:00:06.263
and the first set of gaps is
about the package itself.

3
00:00:06.263 --> 00:00:09.754
The compiled file records who
built it, on which machine,

4
00:00:09.754 --> 00:00:13.701
and where, and that file goes to
storage the whole fleet can read.

5
00:00:13.701 --> 00:00:17.941
Compiling twice gives different
bytes, and so does packaging twice,

6
00:00:17.941 --> 00:00:20.894
so a reviewer can't tell
a real change from noise,

7
00:00:20.894 --> 00:00:24.075
and a rebuilt package won't
match the reviewed hash.

8
00:00:24.075 --> 00:00:25.875
Nothing scans for secrets.

9
00:00:25.875 --> 00:00:27.663
And module versions float.

10
00:00:27.663 --> 00:00:31.200
Each gap has a fix in the
example, pinned by a test.
